# CODEOWNERS: who reviews changes to each part of WING.
#
# When a pull request changes a file, GitHub asks that file's owners to
# review it. With "Require review from Code Owners" turned on in the branch
# protection rule, the pull request can't merge until one of them approves.
# GitHub reads this file from the pull request's base branch.
#
# Every rule below is switched off (commented out) until the owners are
# known. To fill it in:
#   1. Replace each OWNER-... placeholder with a GitHub @username. Teams
#      (@organisation/team-name) only work once the repo moves to a GitHub
#      organisation; then the yearly handover only changes who is in the
#      team, not this file.
#   2. Delete the "# " in front of each rule you want to switch on.
#   3. Give every owner write access to the repo (a team must also be
#      visible). GitHub skips owners it can't use; open this file on
#      github.com afterwards to see any errors.
#
# Placeholders:
#   OWNER-LEADS         all leads: anything no other rule covers (README,
#                       TASKS.md, docs/)
#   OWNER-REPO-CONFIG   repo-wide config in the root folder
#   OWNER-CI            CI workflows, these review rules, the PR template
#   OWNER-FRONTEND      the React app in frontend/
#   OWNER-POSITIONING   QR codes and positioning (inside frontend/)
#   OWNER-DATABASE      Supabase migrations, seed data and Edge Functions
#   OWNER-OSM           the OpenStreetMap import and its snapshot
#
# Patterns work like .gitignore, except that "!" and "[ ]" don't work.
# The LAST rule that matches a file wins, so general rules come first.

# Anything not matched by a later rule
# *                                           OWNER-LEADS

# Root config
# /.gitignore                                 OWNER-REPO-CONFIG
# /.gitattributes                             OWNER-REPO-CONFIG
# /.editorconfig                              OWNER-REPO-CONFIG
# /.nvmrc                                     OWNER-REPO-CONFIG
# /.vscode/                                   OWNER-REPO-CONFIG

# CI, CODEOWNERS and the pull request template
# /.github/                                   OWNER-CI

# The React app
# /frontend/                                  OWNER-FRONTEND

# QR codes and positioning: the positioning lead's files inside frontend/
# /frontend/src/screens/ScanScreen.tsx        OWNER-POSITIONING
# /frontend/src/components/QRScanner.tsx      OWNER-POSITIONING
# /frontend/src/hooks/useQrScanner.ts         OWNER-POSITIONING
# /frontend/src/repositories/qrRepository.ts  OWNER-POSITIONING

# Database: schema, Row Level Security, seed data, Edge Functions
# /backend/supabase/                          OWNER-DATABASE

# OpenStreetMap import, snapshot and survey list
# /backend/osm/                               OWNER-OSM
